Can you hang on for a second?

721
00:44:40,611 --> 00:44:42,272
-Sure.
-Thank you.

722
00:44:42,946 --> 00:44:43,776
Hello.

723
00:44:43,847 --> 00:44:46,941
Mr. Deeds, this is Kevin Ward,
the quarterback you punched.

724
00:44:47,418 --> 00:44:48,680
What's up, buddy?

725
00:44:49,019 --> 00:44:53,956
I wanted to say that I was thinking it over
and I'd like to live up to my word.

726
00:44:54,224 --> 00:44:56,021
And I'd like to win you a Super Bowl.

727
00:44:56,093 --> 00:44:58,721
-That's terrific, pal.
-And my daddy wants to speak to you.

728
00:45:00,164 --> 00:45:02,257
Deeds. Buddy Ward here, Kevin's daddy.

729
00:45:02,566 --> 00:45:03,658
How you doing, Mr. Ward?

730
00:45:03,901 --> 00:45:06,301
I just want to thank you
for teaching my boy a lesson.

731
00:45:06,370 --> 00:45:10,272
He's a good kid. He just has to watch
his language in front of ladies.

732
00:45:13,477 --> 00:45:15,035
I'll remind Kevin where he comes from.

733
00:45:15,679 --> 00:45:16,941
That sounds terrific.

734
00:45:17,214 --> 00:45:20,342
You used foul language in front of a lady?

735
00:45:21,118 --> 00:45:22,142
No, Daddy, no!

736
00:45:26,490 --> 00:45:27,218
Pam.

737
00:45:27,691 --> 00:45:28,623
Still here.

738
00:45:28,959 --> 00:45:30,221
How's it going? You at work?

739
00:45:30,661 --> 00:45:33,824
-Yep, here in the nurse's office.
-Any customers?

740
00:45:34,631 --> 00:45:36,792
