I'm coming!

1198
01:17:19,901 --> 01:17:22,597
Go down! Go down!

1199
01:17:22,671 --> 01:17:24,571
Here comes the black foot.

1200
01:17:26,608 --> 01:17:27,597
No!

1201
01:17:31,313 --> 01:17:33,611
I know it's gross, but grab it.

1202
01:17:38,186 --> 01:17:40,313
I got you. I got you.

1203
01:17:40,756 --> 01:17:45,489
-Oh, God, your foot is disgusting!
-I know, I know. Come here.

1204
01:17:45,994 --> 01:17:48,588
Come on, you okay? You okay?

1205
01:17:49,297 --> 01:17:50,525
I think so.

1206
01:17:54,069 --> 01:17:56,902
You didn't really fall out of an apple tree,
did you?

1207
01:17:58,907 --> 01:17:59,896
No.

1208
01:18:02,544 --> 01:18:04,068
But I really love you.

1209
01:18:06,181 --> 01:18:08,308
I don't even know who you are.

1210
01:18:09,384 --> 01:18:10,681
I'm sorry.

1211
01:18:37,279 --> 01:18:39,110
I am so sorry.

1212
01:18:47,089 --> 01:18:51,549
A company in tatters. Preston Blake's
great legacy gone to the highest bidder.

1213
01:18:51,626 --> 01:18:55,357
The shocking announcement from Chuck Cedar
today confirmed that Blake Media...

1214
01:18:55,430 --> 01:18:58,297
...will be stripped down
and sold off piece by piece.

1215
01:18:58,633 --> 01:19:02,000
The only man who could stand up
to Mr. Cedar and save the company...

1216
01:19:02,070 --> 01:19:06,598
...Longfellow Deeds, has apparently
given up his voting rights and left the city.

1217
01:19:07,109 --> 01:19:09,771
The sale's expected to pass
with unanimous consent...

1218
01:19:09,845 --> 01:19:13,804
...at the annual stockholders' meeting
here in New York tomorrow afternoon.

1219
01:19:14,249 --> 01:19:17,844
Sources indicate that virtually
all of Blake's 50,000 employees...

1220
01:19:17,919 --> 01:19:20,387
...are likely to lose their jobs.

1221
01:19:20,455 --> 01:19:22,514
Wait a minute. I'm a Blake employee.

1222
01:19:23,258 --> 01:19:26,022
Holy shit! This sucks.

1223
01:19:27,129 --> 01:19:30,929
Ladies and gentlemen,
the bottom line is that this divestiture...

1224
01:19:30,999 --> 01:19:35,993
...will result in every shareholder,
all of you and myself included...

1225
01:19:36,404 --> 01:19:39,373
...getting a substantial premium for our shares.

1226
01:19:41,209 --> 01:19:44,838
But before we vote, the company bylaws
require me to open the floor...

1227
01:19:44,913 --> 01:19:48,713
...to shareholders for statements
either for or against this buyout plan.

1228
01:19:49,117 --> 01:19:51,210
Does anyone wish to make a statement?

1229
01:19:51,686 --> 01:19:55,247
Dismantling this company
would be an insult to a great man.

1230
01:19:56,091 --> 01:19:57,149
You scared me.

1231
01:19:57,592 --> 01:20:01,756
It is an unspeakable outrage
and it cannot be allowed to happen.

1232
01:20:05,600 --> 01:20:07,795
Excuse me. I got a statement.

1233
01:20:10,572 --> 01:20:12,130
Longfellow Deeds.

1234
01:20:12,207 --> 01:20:15,233
Unfortunately, since you sold me
your 300 million shares...

1235
01:20:15,310 --> 01:20:18,746
-...you've no right to speak at this meeting.
-Unfortunately for you...

1236
01:20:18,814 --> 01:20:21,544
...I bought one share of Blake Media
this morning.

1237
01:20:21,616 --> 01:20:24,380
You told me every stockholder
has a say in this company.

1238
01:20:24,753 --> 01:20:26,311
Even the little guy.

1239
01:20:28,657 --> 01:20:33,060
You have two minutes, but remember,
I control 49 percent of this company.

1240
01:20:33,128 --> 01:20:36,256
You're gonna have to persuade
just about everyone else...

1241
01:20:36,331 --> 01:20:37,821
...to start hating money.

1242
01:20:45,607 --> 01:20:47,802
Hello, everybody. I'm Deeds.

1243
01:20:48,710 --> 01:20:51,804
For a little while, I was a big part of this company.

1244
01:20:52,414 --> 01:20:54,678
I was wicked rich and powerful.

1245
01:20:55,450 --> 01:20:58,180
Now being rich and powerful isn't a bad thing.

1246
01:20:59,321 --> 01:21:03,223
It looks like the Monopoly guy over there
is pretty darned psyched about it.

1247
01:21:04,226 --> 01:21:07,252
But the problem is
what can happen when you decide...

1248
01:21:07,329 --> 01:21:11,698
...that you would do absolutely anything
to become rich and powerful.

1249
01:21:11,766 --> 01:21:14,633
I don't know who licked the red off
your lollipop today...

1250
01:21:14,703 --> 01:21:17,035
...but you are preaching to the wrong choir.

1251
01:21:17,372 --> 01:21:19,533
All I'm saying is, when you were kids...

1252
01:21:19,608 --> 01:21:22,805
...did you dream
about becoming a savvy investor one day...

1253
01:21:23,078 --> 01:21:25,979
...who would think with his wallet
instead of his heart?

1254
01:21:27,148 --> 01:21:28,979
Come on, I know I didn't.

1255
01:21:29,484 --> 01:21:31,213
I wanted to be a fireman.

1256
01:21:32,020 --> 01:21:35,387
I wanted to be the guy everybody called on
if they were in trouble.

1257
01:21:35,824 --> 01:21:37,382
I wanted to help people...

1258
01:21:37,459 --> 01:21:40,587
...and yeah, I wanted to slide down
those wicked awesome poles.

1259
01:21:41,997 --> 01:21:45,398
But money,
that was the last thing I thought about.

1260
01:21:46,368 --> 01:21:49,462
What about you, sir?
Did you want to be a fireman?

1261
01:21:49,537 --> 01:21:50,868
No, I did not.

1262
01:21:52,407 --> 01:21:54,671
Truth be told, I wanted to be a veterinarian.

1263
01:21:54,743 --> 01:21:57,211
Cool. Why would you want to do that?

1264
01:21:58,079 --> 01:22:01,014
-I wanted to help sick animals.
-And what do you do now?

1265
01:22:01,416 --> 01:22:03,407
I own a chain of slaughterhouses.

1266
01:22:03,852 --> 01:22:06,753
You kind of went the other way
on that one, didn't you?

1267
01:22:07,822 --> 01:22:08,686
Okay.

1268
01:22:08,757 --> 01:22:11,351
In the back. Come on.
Tell me what you wanted to be.

1269
01:22:11,426 --> 01:22:13,656
I wanted to be a magician.

1270
01:22:15,263 --> 01:22:19,324
-And what do you do now?
-I operate a pornographic website.

1271
01:22:20,035 --> 01:22:24,096
That makes people happy also, I guess.
But kind of in a grosser way.

1272
01:22:25,407 --> 01:22:27,739
-Who else?
-I wanted to be a senator.

1273
01:22:28,243 --> 01:22:32,111
-I wanted to be a florist.
-International House Pancake.

1274
01:22:32,647 --> 01:22:34,308
I wanted to be a man.

1275
01:22:36,451 --> 01:22:38,316
That explains a lot.

1276
01:22:38,887 --> 01:22:41,117
I wanted to be a Ping-Pong champion.

1277
01:22:43,959 --> 01:22:46,826
But you're not those things
you wanted to be, are you?

1278
01:22:47,295 --> 01:22:51,129
Everybody made a compromise,
then another compromise, and now...

1279
01:22:51,199 --> 01:22:56,102
...you're about to put 50,000 people out of work,
to make a quick buck? Come on.

1280
01:22:56,604 --> 01:22:59,971
I bet if we ran into the 6th-grade versions
of ourselves right now...

1281
01:23:00,041 --> 01:23:03,033
...they would kick our asses
and put Bubble Yum in our hair...

1282
01:23:03,111 --> 01:23:05,204
...for even thinking about doing this.

1283
01:23:07,415 --> 01:23:10,009
He's right. I would've beat my greedy ass red.

1284
01:23:10,251 --> 01:23:12,617
I would've thrown myself off the merry-go-round.

1285
01:23:12,687 --> 01:23:17,147
I would've tied myself naked to a chair
and burned myself with lit cigarettes.

1286
01:23:18,593 --> 01:23:21,528
Did anyone here dream
of becoming a psychiatrist?

1287
01:23:21,663 --> 01:23:22,857
Just kidding, pal.

1288
01:23:23,832 --> 01:23:26,630
There's still hope for the kids inside of all of us.

1289
01:23:26,701 --> 01:23:29,169
Please don't break up my uncle's company.

1290
01:23:31,539 --> 01:23:33,200
I always wanted to do that.

1291
01:23:44,019 --> 01:23:45,008
Well...

1292
01:23:46,087 --> 01:23:47,918
...that was very touching, Deeds.

1293
01:23:49,057 --> 01:23:51,287
It appears this divestiture has been defeated.

1294
01:23:51,960 --> 01:23:53,825
Unless I'm forgetting something.

1295
01:23:55,296 --> 01:23:56,923
My 300 million votes...

1296
01:23:56,998 --> 01:24:00,900
...plus the five million votes I control
as proxy for the foreign investors.

1297
01:24:00,969 --> 01:24:03,164
So which way should I vote my 51 percent?

1298
01:24:04,839 --> 01:24:06,067
I vote aye.

1299
01:24:06,674 --> 01:24:08,869
305 million times.

1300
01:24:10,145 --> 01:24:14,013
The ayes have it. And Blake Media is no more.

1301
01:24:14,082 --> 01:24:15,879
Not so fast, Chuck.

1302
01:24:17,218 --> 01:24:20,517
Too bad for you, when I was a kid,
I wanted to be a good reporter.

1303
01:24:20,588 --> 01:24:23,352
Miss Bennett,
I wasn't aware you were a stockholder.

1304
01:24:23,425 --> 01:24:25,586
There's a couple things you're not aware of.

1305
01:24:25,660 --> 01:24:28,185
How to tweeze your eyebrows, for instance.

1306
01:24:28,696 --> 01:24:33,224
Also, when Deeds gave away his fortune,
he gave away something that wasn't his.

1307
01:24:34,669 --> 01:24:39,129
-What are you talking about?
-I have here the diary of Preston Blake.

1308
01:24:42,010 --> 01:24:43,443
I stole it and read it.

1309
01:24:43,511 --> 01:24:46,810
Please don't be mad at me.
I did it for good reasons, I promise.

1310
01:24:47,182 --> 01:24:50,151
I would like to read a passage
from Mr. Blake's diary...

1311
01:24:50,418 --> 01:24:52,978
...dated April 12, 1957.

1312
01:24:53,955 --> 01:24:56,253
"I am a volcano of lust.

1313
01:24:56,391 --> 01:25:00,157
"I've gotten this far in business
by following my heart.

1314
01:25:00,628 --> 01:25:02,357
"And I must follow it now...

1315
01:25:02,931 --> 01:25:04,228
"...in love.

1316
01:25:05,967 --> 01:25:09,425
"If she just gives me a sign, an opening."

1317
01:25:09,804 --> 01:25:12,671
Want me to wipe the leaves
on your ficus tree, Mr. Blake?

1318
01:25:14,275 --> 01:25:16,004
You can call me Preston.

1319
01:25:18,046 --> 01:25:21,743
Want me to wipe the leaves
on your ficus tree, Preston?

1320
01:25:23,451 --> 01:25:24,440
Yes.

1321
01:25:26,588 --> 01:25:27,577
Yes.

1322
01:25:28,490 --> 01:25:29,479
Yes!

1323
01:25:30,692 --> 01:25:32,592
Who was this mystery woman?

1324
01:25:32,827 --> 01:25:37,457
I have here the Blake Media ledger
sign-in book from April, 1957.

1325
01:25:38,133 --> 01:25:43,196
On the night of the 12th, there was
only one woman working on Blake's floor.

1326
01:25:43,638 --> 01:25:48,098
Sadly, nine months later, she died,
giving birth to a son.

1327
01:25:48,676 --> 01:25:50,166
A son born...

1328
01:25:50,445 --> 01:25:53,380
...January 23, 1958.

1329
01:25:54,115 --> 01:25:55,480
That is my birthday.

1330
01:25:55,817 --> 01:25:57,978
To Miss Consuela Lopez.

1331
01:25:58,553 --> 01:25:59,986
That is my mother.

1332
01:26:00,155 --> 01:26:02,885
And the rightful heir to $40 billion!

1333
01:26:03,324 --> 01:26:04,814
That is my money?

1334
01:26:05,026 --> 01:26:07,494
A simple DNA test will show...

1335
01:26:07,629 --> 01:26:11,690
...that Emilio Lopez is the majority stockholder
to Blake Media.

1336
01:26:11,933 --> 01:26:14,060
-It is my money!
-That's your money!

1337
01:26:14,235 --> 01:26:15,759
That is my money!

1338
01:26:17,372 --> 01:26:18,771
Way to go, Emilio!

1339
01:26:19,040 --> 01:26:21,440
I will do good things for everyone.

1340
01:26:21,943 --> 01:26:24,173
Free flamenco lessons for all.

1341
01:26:24,279 --> 01:26:26,338
People, people! Please!

1342
01:26:26,514 --> 01:26:30,006
-That is my money.
-Don't be misled. These are all lies.

1343
01:26:30,385 --> 01:26:31,682
Mr. Cedar...

1344
01:26:32,487 --> 01:26:33,647
...you are fired.

1345
01:26:34,122 --> 01:26:35,851
You can't fire me!

1346
01:26:36,424 --> 01:26:37,891
I'm in control!

1347
01:26:38,259 --> 01:26:40,022
Get your hands off me! I'm Chuck Cedar!

1348
01:26:40,662 --> 01:26:42,425
At the lake, when you saved my life...

1349
01:26:42,497 --> 01:26:45,159
...which I never got a chance
to properly thank you for--

1350
01:26:45,233 --> 01:26:47,758
-You're welcome.
-You said you didn't know who I was.

1351
01:26:47,835 --> 01:26:50,326
And it made me realize I don't know who I am.

1352
01:26:50,505 --> 01:26:53,770
So I started working on it
and here's what I got so far.

1353
01:26:54,275 --> 01:26:57,733
My name is Babe Bennett.
I grew up in Syossett, Long lsland.

1354
01:26:57,879 --> 01:27:01,838
I have brown eyes and I don't know
what my natural hair color is anymore.

1355
01:27:02,217 --> 01:27:05,380
When I was in 5th grade,
I got a crush on Walter Cronkite.

1356
01:27:05,453 --> 01:27:09,048
And I really did have that Holly Hobby notebook
I was telling you about.

1357
01:27:09,157 --> 01:27:13,218
I love Bruce Springsteen, Almond Roca
and Abbott and Costello movies.

1358
01:27:13,461 --> 01:27:15,520
I don't like licorice or my ankles.

1359
01:27:16,097 --> 01:27:19,260
More importantly,
I know that I messed up real bad.

1360
01:27:19,434 --> 01:27:22,130
And I'd be willing to spend the rest of my life...

1361
01:27:22,503 --> 01:27:24,801
...begging you to give me another chance...

1362
01:27:24,973 --> 01:27:27,271
...because I am so deeply in love with you...

1363
01:27:28,376 --> 01:27:31,812
...and I know it's definitely
that forever kind of love--

1364
01:27:31,879 --> 01:27:33,210
You're crazy.

1365
01:27:35,650 --> 01:27:37,140
You have beautiful ankles.

1366
01:27:47,695 --> 01:27:49,162
Let's go home.

1367
01:27:51,633 --> 01:27:54,363
You're fired! You! You!

1368
01:27:54,669 --> 01:27:57,160
Oh, you, sir. You are definitely fired.

1369
01:27:57,805 --> 01:28:02,765
I'd like to stay. I think I can really do
some good if I just got another chance.

1370
01:28:06,481 --> 01:28:10,508
Not fired. But tomorrow morning,
you let me change your socks.

1371
01:28:12,153 --> 01:28:13,142
Okay.

1372
01:28:14,455 --> 01:28:17,549
And you, Long-Long-Longfellow...

1373
01:28:17,925 --> 01:28:21,224
...you are the one who made all this possible...

1374
01:28:21,296 --> 01:28:24,288
...with your beautiful words
and your beautiful spirit.

1375
01:28:24,632 --> 01:28:27,430
And Miss Bennett, with her beautiful research.

1376
01:28:27,969 --> 01:28:29,402
How can I thank you?

1377
01:28:29,804 --> 01:28:32,967
All I want is your friendship, Emilio.
You're a good man.

1378
01:28:34,208 --> 01:28:35,402
I'll miss you.

1379
01:28:36,844 --> 01:28:37,833
Deeds!

1380
01:28:39,147 --> 01:28:41,980
-How about $1 billion?
-All right.

1381
01:28:42,517 --> 01:28:43,415
Done.

1382
01:28:56,297 --> 01:28:57,355
Holy Jeez!

1383
01:28:58,166 --> 01:28:59,633
I can't believe it!

1384
01:29:00,201 --> 01:29:02,601
-What's that?
-A letter from Hallmark.

1385
01:29:02,670 --> 01:29:05,161
They're actually going to buy one of my cards.

1386
01:29:05,273 --> 01:29:09,334
-My gosh! Which one?
-The one I wrote for you, remember it?

1387
01:29:09,977 --> 01:29:11,376
Do I remember?

1388
01:29:12,046 --> 01:29:14,913
"Hard to breathe, feels like floating

1389
01:29:15,416 --> 01:29:18,010
"So full of love my heart's exploding

1390
01:29:18,286 --> 01:29:21,312
"Mouth is dry, hands are shaking

1391
01:29:21,723 --> 01:29:24,021
"My heart is yours for the taking

1392
01:29:24,492 --> 01:29:26,790
"Acting weird, not myself

1393
01:29:27,261 --> 01:29:29,855
"Dancing around like the Keebler elf

1394
01:29:30,164 --> 01:29:33,224
"Finally time for this poor schlub

1395
01:29:34,769 --> 01:29:37,897
"to know how it feels to fall in lub"

1396
01:29:38,506 --> 01:29:39,803
I'm so proud of you!

1397
01:29:45,880 --> 01:29:48,644
Can you believe Deeds bought us all these?

1398
01:29:53,221 --> 01:29:55,052
Damn, these things are fast!

1399
01:29:59,427 --> 01:30:00,724
I'm okay!

1400
01:30:01,763 --> 01:30:02,661
Subtitle Revised by HchC

